  [24.2c vp vg = c^2 at w = 10.0 wp; vg < c < vp] OK
  (d) e.g. fp = 6 MHz, f = 10 MHz: vg = 2.4e+08 < c -> message slower than in vacuum
  (e) dbeta/domega at 24.1's carrier = 5.55556e-09 s/m = 1/vg (not a speed)

==============================================================================
24.3 Name four polarizations
==============================================================================
  (a) 2 sin(wt-bz) x + 2 cos(wt-bz) y: travel u = [0. 0. 1.] (check True); circular, left-handed; |E| max 2, min 2
  (b) 3 cos(wt+bx) y - 3 sin(wt+bx) z: travel u = [-1. -0. -0.] (check True); circular, right-handed; |E| max 3, min 3
  (c) 2 sin(wt-by) z - 2 sin(wt-by) x: travel u = [0. 1. 0.] (check True); linear, --handed; |E| max 2.82843, min 0
  (d) 4 cos(wt-bz) x + 4 cos(wt-bz-pi/3) y: travel u = [0. 0. 1.] (check True); elliptical, right-handed; |E| max 4.89898, min 2.82843
  [24.3a left circular] OK
  [24.3b right circular] OK
  [24.3c linear] OK
  [24.3d right elliptical] OK
  (a) at z=0: E(0) = [0. 2. 0.]  E(T/4) = [2. 0. 0.]
  (b) at x=0: E(0) = [0. 3. 0.]  E(T/4) = [ 0.  0. -3.]
  (c) direction of the line: (z - x)/sqrt2; E(T/4) = [-2.  0.  2.]
  (d) E(0) = [4. 2. 0.]  E(T/4) = [0.       3.464102 0.      ]
  (a) phasor: [0.-2.j 2.+0.j 0.+0.j] = -2j (x + j y) e^{-j b z}: True
  [24.3a phasor -2j(x + jy)] OK
  (d) phasor: 4x + 4 e^{-j pi/3} y, phi = -60 deg, sin(phi) = -0.8660254037844386
  (d) semi-axes: max |E| = 4.898979 (= 4 sqrt(3/2) = 4.898979), min = 2.828428 (= 4 sqrt(1/2) = 2.828427)

